WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.165 --> 00:00:18.677
May 17 Dear Daddy Longlegs, This letter will be very short.

2
00:00:19.998 --> 00:00:23.261
My hand aches from taking notes in class and writing my novel.

3
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:27.364
Graduation is in three weeks.

4
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:31.548
I think you should come and introduce yourself to me.

5
00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:37.755
Julia is inviting Jervie, and Sallie's inviting Jimmy.

6
00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:40.797
But who can I invite?

7
00:00:43.559 --> 00:00:44.700
Just you and Mrs.

8
00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.581
Lippett, and I don't want her here.

9
00:00:48.082 --> 00:00:48.883
Please come.

10
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:50.765
I'll hate you if you don't.

11
00:00:52.666 --> 00:01:04.709
Yours, with love and writer's cramp, Judy June 19 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I'm officially a college graduate!

12
00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:10.970
My diploma is in the bottom drawer of my bureau here at Lock Willow with my two best

13
00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.772
dresses. I was disappointed that you weren't at the graduation ceremony.

14
00:01:17.912 --> 00:01:19.233
But thank you for the roses.

15
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:20.493
They were lovely.

16
00:01:22.754 --> 00:01:25.074
We were getting dressed for the ceremony when they arrived.

17
00:01:25.094 --> 00:01:29.836
"Another box of flowers for you, Judy!"

18
00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:30.836
Sallie said.

19
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.081
"That makes three.

20
00:01:33.521 --> 00:01:34.121
One from Jimmy.

21
00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.262
One from Jervis.

22
00:01:35.362 --> 00:01:36.362
And now this one."

23
00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:42.886
get more flowers than anyone I know."

24
00:01:44.287 --> 00:01:47.448
Julia peeked over my shoulder, trying to see who they were from.

25
00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:52.331
I read the card and announced, "These are from my guardian, Mr.

26
00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:58.074
Smith." "I still don't understand why Uncle Jervis sent you roses," Julia went on.

27
00:02:00.075 --> 00:02:01.276
I smiled to myself.

28
00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.002
"Probably just because I'm your roommate."

29
00:02:05.964 --> 00:02:09.987
"I'm Julia's roommate too, and he didn't send me flowers," Sallie said.

30
00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:13.651
"Not that I need any more flowers.

31
00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:15.893
Jimmy's are enough for me.

32
00:02:17.715 --> 00:02:20.497
Whose flowers are you going to carry in the procession, Judy?"

33
00:02:20.517 --> 00:02:23.560
"Oh, I hadn't thought about that."

34
00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:27.104
Julia had already moved on to other things.

35
00:02:29.044 --> 00:02:32.647
"I hate these horrible black caps and gowns we have to wear.

36
00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:35.890
What's the point of a new dress if it's hidden?"

37
00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.954
"I think we're all supposed to look alike."

38
00:02:41.535 --> 00:02:42.396
Sallie turned to me.

39
00:02:42.416 --> 00:02:44.818
"Have you decided on your flowers?

40
00:02:45.758 --> 00:02:47.120
We have to leave in a few minutes."

41
00:02:52.244 --> 00:02:53.965
"Yes, I'll carry Mr.

42
00:02:54.025 --> 00:02:56.888
Smith's and put the others in some water in the bathtub."

43
00:02:58.368 --> 00:02:59.149
And so, Mr.

44
00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:04.213
Smith, it was your roses that had the honor of accompanying me to graduation.

45
00:03:06.555 --> 00:03:08.817
I only wish you had been there to see me.

46
00:03:10.098 --> 00:03:12.540
I'm at the farm for the summer—maybe forever.

47
00:03:14.021 --> 00:03:17.003
All I want are peace and quiet and lots of time to write.

48
00:03:18.685 --> 00:03:19.765
And I have that here.

49
00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.009
Jervie is coming for a week or so in August.

50
00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.592
Jimmy McBride is going to drop by sometime this summer.

51
00:03:29.192 --> 00:03:33.535
I wish you would arrive in your car, but I know that's a hopeless dream.

52
00:03:35.457 --> 00:03:38.439
Sincerely yours, Judy Abbott, B.A.

53
00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.703
P.S. Aren't you proud to see bachelor of arts after my name?

54
00:03:45.204 --> 00:03:46.645
It looks so official.

55
00:03:49.066 --> 00:03:54.250
July 24 Dear Daddy Longlegs, It's so much fun to work.

56
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.572
(Maybe you don't know that.

57
00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:58.948
Do you even work at all?)

58
00:04:00.729 --> 00:04:03.710
It's especially fun when you're doing something that makes you happy.

59
00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.791
Every day I write as fast as my pen can go.

60
00:04:10.632 --> 00:04:14.793
My only problem is that there aren't enough hours in the day to work on my book.

61
00:04:15.853 --> 00:04:19.814
Did I tell you that Amos, the farmhand, married Carrie, the maid, in May?

62
00:04:21.775 --> 00:04:24.115
I think marriage has ruined their relationship.

63
00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.821
The other day he tracked mud on the floor.

64
00:04:28.841 --> 00:04:32.684
"Look what you've done, Amos!"

65
00:04:33.144 --> 00:04:34.324
Carrie scolded him.

66
00:04:34.344 --> 00:04:37.526
"I just washed that floor!"

67
00:04:40.008 --> 00:04:42.049
She used to laugh when he did something like that.

68
00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:46.891
"Go back outside and bring in some wood for the fire," Carrie said.

69
00:04:48.392 --> 00:04:50.293
Amos grumbled something I couldn't hear.

70
00:04:51.794 --> 00:04:54.816
He used to do anything she asked, but no more.

71
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.937
Looking at them, I vowed never to marry.

72
00:05:01.938 --> 00:05:03.899
Jimmy McBride came for dinner last Sunday.

73
00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.800
I was so glad to see him.

74
00:05:07.921 --> 00:05:10.822
He reminded me that there's a whole world beyond this farm.

75
00:05:12.163 --> 00:05:14.884
Jimmy travels around selling bonds to banks.

76
00:05:14.904 --> 00:05:19.265
"How did it go with the bank in town?"

77
00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:21.406
I asked as we sat down to dinner.

78
00:05:21.426 --> 00:05:25.308
"They weren't interested in the bonds at all."

79
00:05:27.933 --> 00:05:28.713
Jimmy sighed.

80
00:05:28.733 --> 00:05:31.195
"I'm not having much luck as a salesman."

81
00:05:32.876 --> 00:05:35.999
I think he's too nice to be successful in the financial world.

82
00:05:36.019 --> 00:05:41.322
"If this job doesn't suit you, perhaps you could work for your father," I said.

83
00:05:41.342 --> 00:05:45.465
"That's the last thing I want to do!"

84
00:05:46.586 --> 00:05:49.008
Jimmy seemed so unhappy about his job.

85
00:05:50.989 --> 00:05:52.150
I'm glad he enjoyed Mrs.

86
00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.931
Semple's fried chicken and ice cream.

87
00:05:56.928 --> 00:05:58.809
The postman has just brought us some news.

88
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.672
Jervie will arrive next Friday and spend a week here.

89
00:06:03.933 --> 00:06:05.254
That's something to look forward to.

90
00:06:06.615 --> 00:06:08.957
But I'm afraid my poor book will suffer.

91
00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:12.880
Jervie is a very time-consuming guest.

92
00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:23.968
Yours as always, Judy September 19 Dear Daddy Longlegs, Something has happened, and I need some advice.

93
00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.767
Would it be possible for me to see you?

94
00:06:28.029 --> 00:06:30.192
It's so much easier to talk than write.

95
00:06:32.636 --> 00:06:35.180
Also I don't want your secretary reading my letter.

96
00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.305
Judy P.S.

97
00:06:38.806 --> 00:06:40.008
I'm very unhappy.
